00:07:52.680 --> 00:08:03.240
Because this episode begins so dramatically, we felt like we needed to speak with the woman at the center of this episode.

174
00:08:04.020 --> 00:08:04.620
Absolutely.

175
00:08:04.740 --> 00:08:09.260
We need to talk to Kate Flannery about getting hit by that car.

176
00:08:09.760 --> 00:08:10.360
Yes.

177
00:08:10.360 --> 00:08:13.440
So, guys, Kate chatted with us.

178
00:08:13.580 --> 00:08:15.080
Sam, will you play the interview?

179
00:08:18.480 --> 00:08:22.120
Kate Flannery is here today, you guys, with her tiny teacup.

180
00:08:24.240 --> 00:08:25.080
Hi, Kate.

181
00:08:25.180 --> 00:08:25.820
How are you?

182
00:08:26.000 --> 00:08:26.360
I'm great.

183
00:08:26.380 --> 00:08:27.160
How are you guys doing?

184
00:08:27.180 --> 00:08:28.280
It's so nice to see you.

185
00:08:28.360 --> 00:08:30.380
Wait, we have to get a picture of you with that teacup.

186
00:08:30.580 --> 00:08:31.660
Cody, will you take a picture?

187
00:08:32.880 --> 00:08:33.940
It's not tiny.

188
00:08:33.960 --> 00:08:35.680
It's a regular-sized teacup.

189
00:08:35.680 --> 00:08:36.800
What's tiny about that?

190
00:08:36.840 --> 00:08:37.660
I don't believe you.

191
00:08:37.740 --> 00:08:38.320
It looks tiny.

192
00:08:38.600 --> 00:08:39.160
It's regular.

193
00:08:39.760 --> 00:08:40.860
Oh, my gosh.

194
00:08:40.860 --> 00:08:43.260
And you have a little cup and saucer.

195
00:08:43.860 --> 00:08:44.180
I do.

196
00:08:44.180 --> 00:08:44.920
Here's the thing, guys.

197
00:08:45.040 --> 00:08:48.040
Kate Flannery is one of the classiest gals.

198
00:08:48.280 --> 00:08:50.060
Her home is spectacular.

199
00:08:50.280 --> 00:08:53.600
It is decorated like it's out of Architectural DigeSt.

200
00:08:54.020 --> 00:08:56.020
Every little thing is amazing.

201
00:08:56.020 --> 00:09:01.120
And I am not surprised at all that you look so put together and you're having your tea

202
00:09:01.120 --> 00:09:03.320
in a proper cup and saucer.

203
00:09:03.440 --> 00:09:03.900
Oh, my gosh.

204
00:09:03.960 --> 00:09:04.160
Oh, wait.

205
00:09:04.160 --> 00:09:06.200
But now I got to turn my phone off because someone's calling me.

206
00:09:06.220 --> 00:09:06.270
Sorry, guys.

207
00:09:06.270 --> 00:09:07.520
She's getting an important phone call.

208
00:09:07.920 --> 00:09:08.200
Sorry.

209
00:09:08.260 --> 00:09:08.860
Take it on air.

210
00:09:08.960 --> 00:09:09.420
Take it on air.

211
00:09:09.420 --> 00:09:10.020
Who is it?

212
00:09:10.120 --> 00:09:10.900
Let's talk to them.

213
00:09:10.900 --> 00:09:13.260
I think it was a potential spam, so I hung up on them.

214
00:09:13.300 --> 00:09:13.680
I'm sorry.

215
00:09:13.940 --> 00:09:14.200
Oh, dang it.

216
00:09:14.220 --> 00:09:17.360
I can't get locked in a timeshare just for you for the bit.

217
00:09:17.460 --> 00:09:18.080
I'm sorry, you guys.

218
00:09:18.180 --> 00:09:18.520
I can't.

219
00:09:19.020 --> 00:09:20.280
It's so good to see you.

220
00:09:20.640 --> 00:09:21.240
You don't understand.

221
00:09:21.240 --> 00:09:24.680
We spent every day together for nine years.

222
00:09:24.720 --> 00:09:25.540
I know.

223
00:09:25.920 --> 00:09:26.820
Oh, my God.

224
00:09:26.820 --> 00:09:27.520
I know.

225
00:09:27.940 --> 00:09:30.540
It was so much like a real office job in that respect.

226
00:09:31.320 --> 00:09:31.800
It really was.

227
00:09:31.800 --> 00:09:33.580
Just like hours at our desks.

228
00:09:34.100 --> 00:09:35.400
And the fluorescent light.

229
00:09:35.480 --> 00:09:35.840
Yes.

230
00:09:35.960 --> 00:09:37.740
I mean, that has a real effect on you.

231
00:09:37.840 --> 00:09:38.640
And the snacks.

232
00:09:38.880 --> 00:09:39.420
Come on.

233
00:09:39.540 --> 00:09:40.960
That was the best spread.

234
00:09:41.220 --> 00:09:41.880
Oh, God.

235
00:09:41.880 --> 00:09:43.800
We had the best, best food ever.

236
00:09:43.900 --> 00:09:45.540
It's all my dad ever talked about.

237
00:09:45.540 --> 00:09:49.380
All the years that he visited, and I would pepper him with questions about,

238
00:09:49.380 --> 00:09:51.480
so Steve Carell ate lunch with us today.

239
00:09:51.680 --> 00:09:52.280
Wasn't that great?

240
00:09:52.380 --> 00:09:54.740
And he was like, did you see the steak they had?

241
00:09:55.640 --> 00:09:57.260
It was always about the food.

242
00:09:57.440 --> 00:09:58.200
Bill Kinsey.

243
00:09:58.560 --> 00:09:59.460
Oh, Kate.

244
00:09:59.740 --> 00:10:01.280
It's so good to see you.

245
00:10:01.660 --> 00:10:02.820
And Jenna.

246
00:10:03.160 --> 00:10:03.760
You guys.

247
00:10:04.160 --> 00:10:04.680
You guys.

248
00:10:04.800 --> 00:10:10.180
Kate, we always like to start by asking people how they came to be on The Office.

249
00:10:10.560 --> 00:10:13.240
I actually auditioned for the pilot for the part of Jan.

250
00:10:13.540 --> 00:10:17.300
Allison Jones said, I think you're really right for this show, but I don't know if this

251
00:10:17.300 --> 00:10:17.720
is your part.

252
00:10:17.720 --> 00:10:20.880
So clearly, they went a different way with Melora Harden.

253
00:10:21.460 --> 00:10:23.840
And lo and behold, you guys shot the pilot.

254
00:10:23.940 --> 00:10:28.640
I remember that summer, I was doing a sketch show once a week that was timed.

255
00:10:28.800 --> 00:10:29.820
It was a two-minute sketch show.

256
00:10:29.900 --> 00:10:31.840
So literally, at two minutes, the lights would go out.

257
00:10:31.840 --> 00:10:38.280
It was this live show in Hollywood at this theater on Melrose with one of the Scholar

258
00:10:38.280 --> 00:10:40.900
brothers, Randy, was doing a sketch right before me.

259
00:10:41.040 --> 00:10:43.360
He's like, have you been watching that British show, The Office?

260
00:10:43.380 --> 00:10:44.340
I'm so obsessed with it.

261
00:10:44.460 --> 00:10:46.000
He was like the first person to really tell me about it.

