1511
01:06:47.900 --> 01:06:52.340
If you're looking for it, that's when Michael crawls on top of Meredith.

1512
01:06:52.960 --> 01:07:00.940
Well, now we can go back to The Office, and we are going to find Dwight telling Angela

1513
01:07:00.940 --> 01:07:02.120
some bad news.

1514
01:07:02.120 --> 01:07:03.720
And she's anxious to see him.

1515
01:07:03.860 --> 01:07:05.360
She wants to know how it went.

1516
01:07:05.500 --> 01:07:06.420
You can just tell.

1517
01:07:06.860 --> 01:07:07.260
Yeah.

1518
01:07:07.260 --> 01:07:08.360
And then he's like, hey, monkey.

1519
01:07:08.520 --> 01:07:09.540
And she's like, any problems?

1520
01:07:09.980 --> 01:07:12.520
Well, you left the TV on, and your cat is dead.

1521
01:07:13.160 --> 01:07:15.480
And my character's like, what?

1522
01:07:15.880 --> 01:07:18.720
And he's like, Sparkles, the white one, is dead.

1523
01:07:18.720 --> 01:07:20.600
Yeah, he gets the name wrong.

1524
01:07:20.820 --> 01:07:21.460
It's bad.

1525
01:07:21.580 --> 01:07:22.280
It is bad.

1526
01:07:22.560 --> 01:07:24.020
This will not end well.

1527
01:07:24.740 --> 01:07:30.980
Angela, you get so very immediately emotional, and not in a funny way.

1528
01:07:31.140 --> 01:07:38.260
Like, this is one of the ways that our show allowed characters to be real people, because

1529
01:07:39.300 --> 01:07:44.400
Angela, the character, really loved her cat, and she is heartbroken.

1530
01:07:44.760 --> 01:07:48.060
And you see that real pain here from your character.

1531
01:07:48.060 --> 01:07:50.360
How did you gear up for this scene?

1532
01:07:51.080 --> 01:07:57.140
Well, Greg told me, he said, you know, Angela Martin, hearing this news will be devastated.

1533
01:07:57.740 --> 01:08:05.320
And I need you to play out the beats of hearing news that kind of destroys you in the moment.

1534
01:08:05.480 --> 01:08:10.260
You know, and I feel like we've all had moments in our lives where we've gotten that phone call

1535
01:08:10.260 --> 01:08:12.500
with some bad news, you know, unfortunately.

1536
01:08:12.500 --> 01:08:20.340
Unfortunately, and I just sort of thought about a few of those moments where, you know, at first,

1537
01:08:20.500 --> 01:08:24.400
you're just in total shock where you're not really sure what you heard.

1538
01:08:25.220 --> 01:08:25.660
Yeah.

1539
01:08:25.820 --> 01:08:29.400
And then it's like someone slaps you in the face with the information.

1540
01:08:30.660 --> 01:08:33.980
And then you're trying to make sense of it, but you can't make sense of it.

1541
01:08:34.580 --> 01:08:35.840
It's the unthinkable.

1542
01:08:35.980 --> 01:08:37.440
And it doesn't make sense.

1543
01:08:37.740 --> 01:08:39.680
And your body is doing all of that.

1544
01:08:39.960 --> 01:08:40.820
You're in shock.

1545
01:08:40.980 --> 01:08:41.800
You're sad.

1546
01:08:42.280 --> 01:08:46.160
Your body, your mind is trying to make it right, but you can't make it right.

1547
01:08:46.340 --> 01:08:47.420
You can't figure it out.

1548
01:08:47.560 --> 01:08:49.040
You don't understand why it happened.

1549
01:08:49.040 --> 01:08:53.000
And I was just trying to process through all of that.

1550
01:08:53.440 --> 01:08:56.360
And yeah, that's what I did.

1551
01:08:56.540 --> 01:08:58.700
Did you have to do a lot of takes of that scene?

1552
01:08:58.700 --> 01:08:59.340
Do you remember?

1553
01:08:59.660 --> 01:09:00.580
No, I didn't.

1554
01:09:00.640 --> 01:09:01.920
I was thankful for that.

1555
01:09:02.240 --> 01:09:05.060
In the next scene, your character is still crying.

1556
01:09:05.260 --> 01:09:11.460
She's standing at reception with Pam, and you look like you've been crying for a long time.

1557
01:09:11.900 --> 01:09:17.200
What did you do to get there, to start the scene in a place like that?

1558
01:09:17.200 --> 01:09:21.660
You know, I'm chatty, so my instinct would be, I'm standing by reception with you, would

1559
01:09:21.660 --> 01:09:24.780
be to be hanging out, you know, being part of the bullpen.

1560
01:09:25.020 --> 01:09:29.780
So one of the things I did was I went around the corner by the elevators, by myself, in

1561
01:09:29.780 --> 01:09:31.760
between takes, and I did not hang out.

1562
01:09:32.020 --> 01:09:35.020
And I just tried to stay in sort of that sad space.

1563
01:09:36.700 --> 01:09:43.980
And also, the makeup department, they wanted my eyes to really look like I had bawled my eyes

1564
01:09:43.980 --> 01:09:44.200
out.

1565
01:09:44.340 --> 01:09:45.260
And they did.

1566
01:09:45.260 --> 01:09:48.680
So I had to get myself back in that emotional place and get sad again.

1567
01:09:49.240 --> 01:09:55.940
And also, the makeup department, Kenneth Paul, who did my makeup, did like this type of eyeliner

1568
01:09:55.940 --> 01:10:00.920
that really made the inside, it was like in the inside of your eye, reddish pink.

1569
01:10:01.220 --> 01:10:05.800
So my eyes looked the part, and then emotionally, I got there.

1570
01:10:06.740 --> 01:10:10.420
Your eyes looked like you had three margaritas yesterday.

1571
01:10:11.780 --> 01:10:12.940
That's what you look like.

1572
01:10:13.000 --> 01:10:16.400
Maybe that's what I, that should have been my prep instead of eyeliner and sad thoughts.

1573
01:10:17.420 --> 01:10:23.620
No, what happened was Laverne just showed Kenneth Paul a picture of me from the previous day

1574
01:10:23.620 --> 01:10:25.320
and was like, make her look like that.

1575
01:10:25.760 --> 01:10:30.440
No, but in all seriousness, Angela, when I was watching these series of scenes where your character

1576
01:10:30.440 --> 01:10:37.980
is really, really devastated over the death of Sprinkles, I was just so beyond impressed

1577
01:10:37.980 --> 01:10:42.680
with your performance and your range and your believability.

1578
01:10:43.120 --> 01:10:46.760
It was just, this is just great, great work.

1579
01:10:46.760 --> 01:10:47.880
Aw, thanks.

1580
01:10:47.940 --> 01:10:49.300
I appreciate that.

1581
01:10:49.560 --> 01:10:55.040
I really appreciated Greg writing the storyline for me, and I got to do all these things,

1582
01:10:55.100 --> 01:11:00.720
you know, and, and, you know, his take as a director was always to try to keep it as

1583
01:11:00.720 --> 01:11:01.780
honest as possible.

1584
01:11:02.600 --> 01:11:03.160
Yeah.

1585
01:11:04.120 --> 01:11:11.320
Well, there's another really great moment in this scene, and we actually had a fan write

1586
01:11:11.320 --> 01:11:18.420
in, Katie Harwick said, I think we need to give a shout out to Michael when Angela's cat

1587
01:11:18.420 --> 01:11:18.880
dies.

1588
01:11:19.320 --> 01:11:23.840
Not only did he know her name, but he was overcome with grief.

1589
01:11:24.020 --> 01:11:28.840
He cares so much for his employees, and it was just such a sweet moment to me.

1590
01:11:29.080 --> 01:11:35.900
But I do have to ask, do you think he was truly sad, or did he just see this as a distraction

1591
01:11:35.900 --> 01:11:38.700
from hitting Meredith that everyone could talk about instead?

1592
01:11:38.700 --> 01:11:43.500
Instead, I personally think he was very distraught about sprinkles.

1593
01:11:43.800 --> 01:11:44.840
Well, I agree.

1594
01:11:45.140 --> 01:11:50.580
This happens at 12 minutes, 41 seconds, and it is one of my favorite endearing moments

1595
01:11:50.580 --> 01:11:51.060
of Michael.

1596
01:11:51.200 --> 01:11:55.220
Now, maybe because it's personal for me, because, you know, I played Angela Martin.

1597
01:11:55.320 --> 01:11:56.820
I knew how much she loved her cats.

1598
01:11:57.160 --> 01:12:02.580
But Michael, it's like that moment when the trick-or-treaters come to his house, and you

1599
01:12:02.580 --> 01:12:03.360
see his joy.

1600
01:12:03.620 --> 01:12:07.380
It's like that moment when he shows up to Pam's art show.

1601
01:12:08.060 --> 01:12:08.360
Yeah.

1602
01:12:08.360 --> 01:12:11.960
Michael really saw these people as his family.

1603
01:12:12.220 --> 01:12:14.900
So Michael knew Angela's love of sprinkles.

1604
01:12:15.060 --> 01:12:15.960
Of course he did.

1605
01:12:16.400 --> 01:12:16.960
Yeah.

1606
01:12:16.960 --> 01:12:19.740
And he was gutted to hear that sprinkles died.

1607
01:12:19.940 --> 01:12:24.100
The way he puts his hand up to his face, and he kind of collapses into the wall, and

1608
01:12:24.100 --> 01:12:26.160
he's like, oh, shoot.

1609
01:12:26.560 --> 01:12:28.200
I'm sorry, Angela.

1610
01:12:28.600 --> 01:12:31.040
I mean, could it get any worse?

1611
01:12:31.740 --> 01:12:33.240
He's feeling all of that.

1612
01:12:33.380 --> 01:12:34.680
He really feels bad.

1613
01:12:34.680 --> 01:12:40.780
And now he gets sprinkles' name right the first time, and then he makes a big speech

1614
01:12:40.780 --> 01:12:41.700
and calls her Prinkles.

1615
01:12:42.020 --> 01:12:42.660
So, you know.

1616
01:12:42.780 --> 01:12:43.240
He does.

1617
01:12:43.940 --> 01:12:44.760
That's right.

1618
01:12:45.020 --> 01:12:49.180
He says, so many bad things have happened today.

1619
01:12:49.600 --> 01:12:55.440
The computer crashes from porn, merit of this accident, and now Prinkles.

1620
01:12:55.440 --> 01:12:56.500
We're cursed.

1621
01:12:56.860 --> 01:12:58.340
This seals the deal.

1622
01:12:58.740 --> 01:13:00.520
To him, that's it.

1623
01:13:00.620 --> 01:13:04.760
The office is cursed, and now he's got to figure out how to break this curse.

1624
01:13:05.280 --> 01:13:09.560
Yes, but he does say, I'm not superstitious, but I am a little stitious.

1625
01:13:10.540 --> 01:13:13.000
It's like he thinks they're two separate words.

1626
01:13:13.320 --> 01:13:19.040
Well, we had a fan question about that line from Jessica Williard and Lauren Corwin.

1627
01:13:19.480 --> 01:13:25.420
They said, that line makes me laugh every time who wrote this joke.

1628
01:13:25.620 --> 01:13:26.780
I was curious, too.

1629
01:13:26.900 --> 01:13:27.720
Did you find out?

1630
01:13:28.120 --> 01:13:28.820
I did.

1631
01:13:29.060 --> 01:13:30.460
It was Gene Stupnitsky.

1632
01:13:30.700 --> 01:13:32.120
Gene, hilarious.

1633
01:13:32.820 --> 01:13:37.240
Yeah, I asked Greg, and he said, I'm pretty sure it was Gene or Lee.

1634
01:13:37.240 --> 01:13:38.980
I reached out to those guys.

1635
01:13:39.220 --> 01:13:41.280
Gene said, yes, it was me.

1636
01:13:41.500 --> 01:13:42.180
He remembers.

1637
01:13:42.480 --> 01:13:48.960
They were in a group, and this talking head leads to a commercial break, and they needed

1638
01:13:48.960 --> 01:13:49.500
a button.

1639
01:13:49.560 --> 01:13:55.020
They needed a little button at the end of this talking head so that they could go to commercial,

1640
01:13:55.140 --> 01:13:59.680
and he said they were just trying to come up with something, and all of a sudden, he

1641
01:13:59.680 --> 01:14:01.540
said, he shouted out, I've got it.

1642
01:14:01.760 --> 01:14:04.960
This might be stupid, but how about this?

1643
01:14:04.960 --> 01:14:08.880
And he pitched that line, and it is so genius.

1644
01:14:09.120 --> 01:14:12.800
It is such a good line, and I hear that line quoted all the time.

1645
01:14:12.920 --> 01:14:14.840
It is a Michael Scott classic line.

1646
01:14:15.200 --> 01:14:16.020
It is.

1647
01:14:16.120 --> 01:14:16.680
It's true.

1648
01:14:17.460 --> 01:14:23.080
Well, speaking of classic Michael Scott, we're now going to move into one of Michael's conference

1649
01:14:23.080 --> 01:14:23.840
room meetings.

1650
01:14:24.200 --> 01:14:26.580
This is an epic conference room meeting.

1651
01:14:26.740 --> 01:14:29.160
We were in this conference room all freaking day.

1652
01:14:29.160 --> 01:14:30.940
We got loopy.

1653
01:14:31.120 --> 01:14:31.920
We got punchy.

1654
01:14:32.060 --> 01:14:34.380
I'm going to tell you where we flat out lost it.

1655
01:14:34.760 --> 01:14:35.920
It's so good.

1656
01:14:36.340 --> 01:14:36.520
Yeah.

1657
01:14:36.680 --> 01:14:43.860
I also remember that they very specifically did not seat Jim and Pam next to one another.

1658
01:14:44.020 --> 01:14:50.280
This was part of Jim and Pam's supposed way of deflecting that we're dating.

1659
01:14:51.020 --> 01:14:51.540
Yeah.

1660
01:14:52.080 --> 01:14:56.780
And I remember that you have to just be sad and kind of cry through this scene, and that

1661
01:14:56.780 --> 01:15:01.680
I didn't want to chat you up too much because I knew you had to stay in that space.

1662
01:15:01.880 --> 01:15:02.740
And I did.

1663
01:15:02.900 --> 01:15:03.500
I did.

1664
01:15:04.000 --> 01:15:08.580
I really stayed sad until the end when Steve made me break into laughter.

1665
01:15:08.840 --> 01:15:11.380
So Michael in this scene is questioning his employees.

1666
01:15:11.660 --> 01:15:15.120
He feels like someone must have done something to get this curse, right?

1667
01:15:15.120 --> 01:15:18.780
Like, have they violated an ancient Indian burial ground?

1668
01:15:19.060 --> 01:15:24.480
And then, you know, he wants to know what everyone's religious beliefs are, which Toby

1669
01:15:24.480 --> 01:15:27.240
says, Michael, we can't, you can't do that.

1670
01:15:27.380 --> 01:15:28.420
You can't discuss that.

1671
01:15:28.640 --> 01:15:31.840
Michael calls Toby Satan repeatedly in this scene.

1672
01:15:32.500 --> 01:15:34.980
One, because he won a week of free pizza.

1673
01:15:35.100 --> 01:15:36.480
So he's like, I don't think there's a curse.

1674
01:15:36.640 --> 01:15:37.980
And Michael's like, okay, Satan.

1675
01:15:38.480 --> 01:15:40.120
So he goes around the room.

1676
01:15:40.300 --> 01:15:42.580
Pam and Daryl are both Presbyterians.

1677
01:15:42.880 --> 01:15:43.500
They high five.

1678
01:15:45.120 --> 01:15:48.760
There's this great line where she says, I'm a Lutheran and Bob is a Unitarian.

1679
01:15:49.040 --> 01:15:50.280
Keeps things spicy.

1680
01:15:51.400 --> 01:15:51.800
Mm-hmm.

1681
01:15:52.380 --> 01:15:55.980
Creed said he's been a follower in a cult and a leader in a cult.

1682
01:15:56.160 --> 01:15:58.700
The followers have more fun, but the leaders make more money.

1683
01:15:59.000 --> 01:16:04.320
But Michael has decided he thinks maybe we should do an animal sacrifice.

1684
01:16:04.640 --> 01:16:05.060
Yes.

1685
01:16:05.180 --> 01:16:05.400
You know?

1686
01:16:05.520 --> 01:16:06.480
That's going to do it.

1687
01:16:06.520 --> 01:16:07.160
Maybe that would help.

1688
01:16:07.360 --> 01:16:07.540
Yeah.

1689
01:16:07.700 --> 01:16:07.940
Mm-hmm.

1690
01:16:08.280 --> 01:16:13.780
And then he starts naming animals, but they don't exiSt.

1691
01:16:13.780 --> 01:16:15.380
I wrote them down.

1692
01:16:15.580 --> 01:16:24.280
He suggests that we sacrifice an animal that has the body of a walrus and the head of a sea lion,

1693
01:16:26.500 --> 01:16:31.100
or the body of an egret with the head of a meerkat,

1694
01:16:33.660 --> 01:16:44.320
or maybe one that has the head of a monkey with the antlers of a reindeer and the body of a porcupine.

1695
01:16:45.100 --> 01:16:45.240
Okay.

1696
01:16:45.460 --> 01:16:49.500
Jenna, when Steve started this runner, they just let him go.

1697
01:16:49.720 --> 01:16:50.620
Do you remember this?

1698
01:16:50.860 --> 01:16:51.000
Yes.

1699
01:16:51.000 --> 01:16:54.900
He just started improvising different animal combinations.

1700
01:16:55.280 --> 01:16:58.300
We didn't know what was going to come out of the guy's mouth.

1701
01:16:58.480 --> 01:17:02.860
We all started dropping like flies, cracking up.

1702
01:17:02.980 --> 01:17:06.320
And the other thing is, he would say it with such seriousness.

1703
01:17:06.720 --> 01:17:11.980
And this was the comedy killer, the long pauses.

1704
01:17:11.980 --> 01:17:17.880
He takes such a long pause before he says, body of a porcupine?

1705
01:17:18.360 --> 01:17:18.960
Yes.

1706
01:17:19.180 --> 01:17:20.060
We were on the floor.

1707
01:17:20.240 --> 01:17:21.620
We were on the floor.

1708
01:17:21.800 --> 01:17:27.420
I am not in any background shots while he's doing these animal combinations because I couldn't keep it together.

1709
01:17:27.980 --> 01:17:33.680
And at 18 minutes, 11 seconds, you can see Craig Robinson covering his face.

1710
01:17:33.980 --> 01:17:35.100
I saw it.

1711
01:17:35.380 --> 01:17:36.660
I remember that.

1712
01:17:36.660 --> 01:17:39.280
But we were losing it.

1713
01:17:39.960 --> 01:17:42.600
It was so funny.

1714
01:17:42.820 --> 01:17:45.380
And they let him go for a long time.

1715
01:17:45.900 --> 01:17:48.160
I mean, you are not seeing all of it.

1716
01:17:48.260 --> 01:17:50.040
He went for so long.

1717
01:17:50.220 --> 01:17:55.840
And I remember we were cracking up and we were just like, as a group, we were like, no, get it together.

1718
01:17:56.000 --> 01:17:56.840
These are too good.

1719
01:17:56.940 --> 01:17:57.880
We can't ruin these.

1720
01:17:58.540 --> 01:18:03.900
Well, while all this is happening at the office, Dwight has gone to visit Meredith.

1721
01:18:04.500 --> 01:18:16.280
Meredith, and he has this talking head where he's saying, as he's sitting next to her, that sometimes the best thing to do is to put an animal out of its misery.

1722
01:18:16.640 --> 01:18:17.480
He's a farmer.

1723
01:18:17.780 --> 01:18:18.120
Yeah.

1724
01:18:18.480 --> 01:18:23.480
You could power a small fan for two days with the amount of electricity Meredith is hooked up to.

1725
01:18:24.200 --> 01:18:38.500
I have to say, please, if you go back to rewatch this episode, during this speech by Dwight next to Meredith's bedside, please look at the woman in the bed on the other side.

1726
01:18:39.320 --> 01:18:39.920
Okay?

1727
01:18:40.320 --> 01:18:41.760
Over Dwight's shoulder.

1728
01:18:42.680 --> 01:18:43.800
That's all I'm going to say.

1729
01:18:43.920 --> 01:18:46.940
Just enjoy that performance the next time you watch this scene.

1730
01:18:47.520 --> 01:18:48.580
It's wonderful.

1731
01:18:48.580 --> 01:18:50.040
Oh, my God, Jenna.

1732
01:18:50.400 --> 01:18:53.720
When we were all crammed around Kate's bed, that woman was there.

1733
01:18:55.060 --> 01:19:00.200
I swear, that woman, it was like she was a real patient.

1734
01:19:01.180 --> 01:19:06.060
She let out some kind of noise, and I thought we were all going to shit our pants.

1735
01:19:07.040 --> 01:19:12.480
She was a background actor, but she was so real.

1736
01:19:12.480 --> 01:19:21.000
Well, she literally, while we were standing there one time, went, like, I think they told her to maybe make a moaning sound.

1737
01:19:21.260 --> 01:19:21.540
Yeah.

1738
01:19:21.660 --> 01:19:24.860
And her interpretation of that, we went loopy.

1739
01:19:25.300 --> 01:19:28.500
Well, watch her in the background of the scene because she's excellent.

1740
01:19:28.780 --> 01:19:32.180
So now the doctor comes in, and Dwight has some questions for him.

1741
01:19:32.500 --> 01:19:36.500
And you and I both know that this is our writer, Justin Spitzer.

1742
01:19:38.080 --> 01:19:42.500
Yes, creator of some of your favorite Dwightisms, Justin Spitzer.

1743
01:19:42.780 --> 01:19:44.900
And the creator of the show, Superstore.

1744
01:19:45.300 --> 01:19:50.500
Well, I reached out to Justin, and he told me that he got this role after reading the part in the table read.

1745
01:19:51.480 --> 01:19:53.040
That he made Greg laugh.

1746
01:19:53.180 --> 01:19:55.400
Which Paul Lieberstein has shared that this would happen.

1747
01:19:55.400 --> 01:19:59.260
